    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/alexcrichton\">alexcrichton</a> added the wasi-http label to <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14112\">Issue #14112</a>.</p>",
        "id": 615868718,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1786458782
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14112#issuecomment-5254589297\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14112\">issue #14112</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I suppose the way we're interpreting it in Wasmtime right now is that the future is the result of transmitting the body rather than the entire request, and the result on <code>client::send</code> is the result of sending the request. It wouldn't be too too hard to handle this case within Wasmtime though since the behavior is \"something got dropped\" and we're able to see that and could synthesize a type of error for \"didn't actually succeed\"</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 615869130,
